<title>GERMANY: Broker details Europe 1996 malting barley output.</title>
<headline>Broker details Europe 1996 malting barley output.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring barley output by the EU's leading producers is put at 26.36 million tonnes in 1996 after 19.08 million in 1995, broker Jochen Mautner GmbH said.</p>
<p>The broker put the amount qualifying for malting purposes out of the total crop at 25-30 percent, compared with 35-40 percent last year.</p>
<p>The spring barley area was 6.05 million hectares, up from 5.67 million last year, and average yields rose to 4.35 tonnes per hectare from 3.36 in 1995.</p>
<p>Mautner detailed spring barley output, protein contents and malting barley shares as follows-</p>
<p> OUTPUT in '000 tonnes 1996	  PROTEIN	 MALTING BRLY</p>
<p> (1995 in brackets)		CONTENT IN PCT    SHARE IN PCT</p>
<p> Denmark	   3,180 (2,750) 11.5-12.0 (11.0)  35-40 (45-50)</p>
<p> Germany	   4,176 (2,849)  10.8 (10.8)	   57 (55)</p>
<p> Eng/Wales/N.Ire 1,360 (1,318)  11.5 (11.5)	50-60 (55)</p>
<p> Scotland	  1,610 (1,246) 10.0-11.0 (10.5)  60-65 (65)</p>
<p> Finland	   1,940 (1,725) 10.7-11.3 (11.3)   7-10 (10)</p>
<p> France	    2,698 (2,121)   11.3 (10.6)	  50 (52)</p>
<p> Irish Republic    885   (845)   11.0 (11.4)	  40 (40)</p>
<p> Netherlands	 215   (198)   11.5 (10.4)	  80 (80)</p>
<p> Austria	     840   (625)   10.5 (10.0-12.0)   30 (25-30)</p>
<p> Sweden	    2,100 (1,700) 9.5-11.8 (10.0-12.0) 12-15 (12)</p>
<p> Spain	     7,360 (3,700)   11.5 (12.0-15.0)   10 (5)</p>
<p>Not included in the totals were Poland with 2.86 million tonnes (2.85), 10-12 percent (10.5-12) protein, and a malting barley share of 10-15 percent, as well as the Czech republic with 1.63 million (1.37), 11.5 percent protein (11) and a 30 percent share (35).</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
